            "review_title": "Review at Cafe Goethe",
            "review_text": "mozii\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam69 contributions\n0\nLooks can be deceiving\nApr 2014 • Friends\nAm eating here now as I write the review. The place looks very nice, by Hanoi standards. Colonial building that also houses the German bibliothek and admin centre. Food was priced very decently. Our party of 4 ordered the grilled Aussie beef steak. For VND 500k, it is reasonable. With free flow of bread, what else can a man ask for. \n\nNow comes the beef review. I must admit this is now a case of you get what you pay for. I highly doubt the beef origins and seriously, not fit to be served unless you are a tiger that doesn't look what gets put into your mouth. Lotsa tendons, tough to cut but seasoning was okay.\n\nAlthough I thought I'd return, I doubt so now.\nRead more\nWritten April 26, 2014",
